correctionAndBoundaryPassages.text:
Every authoritative external final response is one UTF-8 JSON file whose top-level object conforms to closed-loop-stage-response/3 and contains exactly:

- schema;
- contractProfileId;
- jobId;
- stage;
- operation;
- promptIdentity;
- packageId;
- operationReservationId;
- challengeNonce;
- scope;
- responseType;
- humanInputRequests;
- humanAuthorityCandidates;
- stageData;
- records;
- evidence;
- unresolved;
- warnings;
- attachments.

promptIdentity is one closed object containing instructionId, bodySha256, contractSha256, and contextSignature. Those values MUST NOT be duplicated at the top level. A compatibility import containing duplicated identity values is historical-only unless every duplicate equals the nested value byte-for-byte and an explicit migration rule removes the duplicates before current validation.

Stage-operation contracts determine the exact required, prohibited, and nullable scope fields. Unknown properties are rejected.

17.2 Prompt identity

promptIdentity.bodySha256 is the SHA-256 of the exact authoritative prompt-file bytes defined in Section 10.1.
promptIdentity.contractSha256 is the SHA-256 of the exact canonical current response contract.
